"""Learning card facts for Japan's 47 prefectures (Japan_plan.md, "More facts"), keyed by the ISO 3166-2:JP number.

Fields (any may be missing; the card leaves out what's missing):
  kanji (the name in kanji)   reading (its romanised reading, with the suffix)   region (one of the 9)   food (famous food
  or meibutsu)   festival   craft (traditional craft)   dialect   high (highest point)   river (main river or lake)
  wonder (natural wonder)   onsen (hot springs)   province (old province names)   castle (famous castle or temple)
  unesco   meaning (what the name means)   industry (known for)   mascot   city (largest city, if it isn't the capital)
The prefectural flower, tree and bird come from each prefecture's English Wikipedia infobox (tools/build_jp.py, SYMBOLS).
Written from general knowledge and the downloaded Wikipedia articles (tools/downloads/jp/wiki/); left out where unsure.
"""

